# Class Rules (topic creation)

## Product
- One lesson = self-contained `classes/NN/index.html` (CSS + JS inline). No build step.
- Target: Slovak grades 8–9, online 1× ~45–60 min. CEFR aim per course: solid **A2 → emerging B1** grammar core (not “all English grammar”).
- Follow Martin worksheet spine: Grammar Review → Listening (4 blocks) → T/F → Scrambled Dialogue → New Topic → Grammar Box → Classroom/Grammar matching.

## Before writing content
Ask only if missing: (1) class number, (2) topic, (3) unit transition, (4) main grammar focus from `curriculum/25-hours.md`.

## Content rules
- Listening: 4 paragraphs, ~80–100 words each; 5 gaps + scrambled 5-word bank per block; full text word-for-word synced with gap text.
- T/F: 8–10 items, factual to listening only.
- Dialogue: 6 Jim questions + Pete scrambled answers; accept flexible order via `DIALOGUE_KEY`.
- Grammar Review must match the hour’s focus and recycle 1–2 prior hours.
- Listening marks the sentences that feed Grammar Review. A **Highlight grammar lines** button (full text and Gap Fill, same toggle) adds `body.gram-on` and colours those spans. The legend names the same groups as section 3 (for example present simple → Review A). Colours stay off until the button is pressed. Mark the same spans in the full text and in the gap text, including around a blank when the missing word sits inside the sentence. Do not add words. `textContent` stays the spoken text, so Listen ignores the marks.
- Optional **Sentence Transformations** pool: per tense 3 lemmas × 3 forms (affirmative/negative/question = 9 sentences); random New set; Check with flexible answers (`don't`/`do not`).
- Matching (last classroom section): **12** English terms → 3 Slovak options each, so the 2-column grid lines up. Slovak stays in the option answers only. Unicode `\u` in JS hint strings.
- Slovak diacritics: prefer `\uXXXX` in JS strings to avoid mojibake.

## UX / app rules
- Desktop web layout (not A4): `.wrap` up to ~1480px; listening / dialogue / matching in 2 columns on wide screens; collapse under 1100px; A4 only in `@media print`.
- Sticky toolbar: first control is `← Home` linking to `../../`; then Show Full Text, Copy controls, Clear Answers.
- **Every task** has its own sticky bar with **Check the answers** and **Clear**. Button labels and instructions are English. Section Clear does not confirm; the global Clear Answers does (`confirm`).
- Check always shows the correct answer: gap/grammar/story/box use `Correct answer: …` after the field; True/False shows `OK` or `X` plus `Correct: T/F`; transforms, dialogue, and matching show `Correct answer:` in the hint even when the student was right.
- Story and Grammar Box checks show a model line (`ok === null`, no red/green). They are not scored.
- Grammar Review hides those answers on the first **input** keystroke (`clearGrammarFeedback`), not on focus. The student checks again to see them.
- Dialogue, transforms, and matching hide check colours when the student edits.
- No `scrollIntoView` jump on check.
- `localStorage` key unique per class: `esl-class-NN-v1`.
- Update root `index.html` hub link when adding a class. Hub preview must cache-bust the iframe (`?v=` + `Date.now()`).

## Listen
- Web Speech API (`speechSynthesis`), `en-GB`. Preferred voices: Google UK English Female/Male, Microsoft Libby/Sonia, Samantha. Speaker button label `Listen`; while that clip plays, the same button is `Stop`.
- Full-text Listen reads all 4 paragraphs **once** at rate `0.92`.
- Gap Fill has one shared bar: Repeat `1×` / `2×` / `3×` (default `1×`) and Speed Slow `0.75` / Normal `0.92` / Fast `1.1` (default Normal). Each block Listen uses those settings. A speed change applies on the next press, not mid-utterance. Pause between repeats is about `900ms` (empty queue item).
- True/False: each subsection has its own Listen. It plays that subsection’s listening paragraphs **twice** at `0.92`, ignoring the Gap Fill Repeat/Speed controls.
- `stopListen` increments a run id so an in-flight `onend` cannot start the next utterance.

## Honesty constraint
Do not promise “full English grammar in 25 hours”. Promise a **recycled functional core** (see curriculum). Each new topic carries old grammar forward.
